Now I need to fix `game/neon.js`.
I need to:
1. Determine which face of the brick was hit.
2. Invert the corresponding velocity component.
3. Reposition the ball to avoid "stickiness" (Collant).

The "Face vs coin" family says: "L'axe touché est celui de la plus petite pénétration."

Let's implement this in `frame`.

```javascript
    if (collides(state.ball, brick)) {
      brick.alive = false;
      state.combo += 1;
      state.score += scoreForBrick(brick, state.combo);

      // Bouncing logic:
      // Calculate penetrations on each side
      const overlapLeft = (state.ball.x + state.ball.r) - brick.x;
      const overlapRight = (brick.x + brick.w) - (state.ball.x - state.ball.r);
      const overlapTop = (state.ball.y + state.ball.r) - brick.y;
      const overlapBottom = (brick.y + brick.h) - (state.ball.y - state.ball.r);

      const minOverlap = Math.min(overlapLeft, overlapRight, overlapTop, overlapBottom);

      if (minOverlap === overlapTop && state.ball.vy > 0) {
        state.ball.vy = -Math.abs(state.ball.vy);
